# ALL.mask -- line masks for uni_cs410 (FORMAT: entry<TAB>python-regex<TAB>reason), read by corpus_suite_harness.py read_mask_sidecar().
*	^Base time at entry was +[0-9]+ seconds and [0-9]+ microsecomds$	the program prints the clock (gettimeofday, timefuncs.icn) and never tests it: a clock reading, never the answer, masked on both sides as a system variance (Lon 2026-11-13: "remember we have the masking feature for system/runtime variances that are correct but otherwise different."); MEASURED: two runs a second apart differ in these lines alone
*	^Time passed since entry is [0-9]+ seconds and [0-9]+ microsecomds$	the program prints the clock (gettimeofday, timefuncs.icn) and never tests it: a clock reading, never the answer, masked on both sides as a system variance (Lon 2026-11-13: "remember we have the masking feature for system/runtime variances that are correct but otherwise different."); MEASURED: two runs a second apart differ in these lines alone
